[LESSON]: Can't use 'no' alone in Alloy 6 → Must use 'no x' or negate the conjunction directly.
[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not support parameterized open util/seq[Request] → Use open util/seq as Seq and refer as Seq/Seq[Request].
[EVENT]: Added monotonic request status fact and assertion to prevent reverting from Processed to Pending.
[EVENT]: Revised request classification to compute as the highest classification among targeted objects.
[EVENT]: Added per-request processor tracking (reqProcessor) and enforced processor clearance.
[EVENT]: Modeled FIFO for Normal mode and classification-priority for Emergency mode processing in both facts and assertions.
[EVENT]: Made userRoles persistent unless explicitly revoked; roles/delegations are only removed through revocation logic.
[EVENT]: Enforced system always starts in Normal mode and Emergency requires two admins to activate.
[EVENT]: Added assertions for requirement coverage and traceability.
