Also, the classification of a request is incorrect in the baseline model. The classification of a request is the the classification of a request is the classification of an object with the highest classification level.
regarding All_requirements, a system always starts out at Normal mode, then it takes 2 administrators triggering the emergency mode at the same time for the system to enter Emergency. EA user can only be assigned or delegated roles that are less than or equal to its clearance. 
Assigned roles should always stay in userRoles.
the system needs to record the user who processed each request. 
The user who processed the request must have higher clearance than the classification level of the request.
the current model does nnot reflect the requirements. check the requirements and update the model accordingly.
- User clarification: 1. All delegated roles assigned during Emergency mode must be revoked immediately upon Emergency exit. Do not revoke the roles delegated during Normal mode (before Emergency mode) as they follow their expiry or they can be revoked early by an administrator.
- User review feedback: 1. allow any user to hold mutual exclusive roles in Emergency.
2. sufficient
3. satified
