The persistent syntax error at the start of pred precedes (line 209) is not due to set comprehension or function definition syntax per se, but rather to the lack of a definition for the predicate Next, which is referenced multiple times in the model (e.g., in facts and assertions) but never actually declared. Alloy 6 requires that all predicates used in the model be defined, even if as stubs. The parser, upon encountering the undefined identifier Next in relational contexts, loses track of the parse state, often reporting the syntax error at the next top-level declaration (here, at pred precedes). Prior fix attempts were focused on function syntax, brace balancing, and comprehension structure, but none addressed the missing Next predicate definition.

